    "https://jobs.jwu.edu/en-us/job/498285/director-of-admissions-charlotte-campus": {
      "title": "Details - Director of Admissions, Charlotte Campus",
      "description": "Details - Director of Admissions, Charlotte Campus arrow arrow drop down email Facebook Play phone play-circle-fill Play quote Shape share YouTube Icon Instagram Twitter About JWU JWU at a Glance Leadership History of JWU Our Alumni Mission Media Center Equity & Compliance Accreditation Resources Academics Majors & Degrees Programs by Campus Colleges Our Faculty Admissions & Aid Paying for College Visit Campus Explore From Home Information Brochures Become a Legacy Family Student Support Services Study Abroad | Global Contact Admissions Campuses Providence Charlotte News Arts & Sciences Business Culinary Arts Engineering & Design Health & Wellness Hospitality Management Student Stories Contact Athletics Apply to JWU Request Information Visit Us Virtual Tour Give to JWU Information For... Information For... Future Students Undergraduate Transfer Graduate Continuing Education International National Student Orgs Early Enrollment Honors Program Legacy Families Military & Veteran Current Students jwuLink Educators Parents & Families Providence Charlotte Alumni JWU Alumni Login A to Z Coronavirus Updates Search Search Search Join our Community Director of Admissions, Charlotte Campus Apply now Job no: 11251 Work type: Full Time Location: Charlotte, North Carolina Categories: Staff/Administration, Admissions, Calendar Year (12-Month), Campus Based Summary Provides strategic and operational leadership for recruitment, admission selection, and enrollment for students at the Charlotte Campus. Develops and executes a data-informed campus admissions plan aligned with university objectives; oversees admissions staff, events, and budget; and partners across the campus and university to strengthen enrollment pipelines, improve conversion and yield, and deliver a positive prospective-student experience Essential Job Functions Creates and implements annual and multi-year campus admissions and recruitment plans, events. Application activity and yield initiatives, to achieve campus enrollment goals; establishes milestones and monitors progress throughout the enrollment cycle Collaborates with others on the Enrollment Management leadership Team to develop a universitywide, data-informed territory management strategy Serves on the enrollment management leadership team and the Charlotte Campus leadership team; advises leaders on admissions performance, market conditions, enrollment trends, risks, and opportunities Collaborates with university admissions and university marketing to develop, execute, successful marketing strategies and campaigns using approved print, email, web, text, phone, social media, and other channels Analyzes enrollment data and recruitment effectiveness to forecast enrollment and adjust recruitment plans, as necessary Manages admissions operations to maintain timely, accurate, and consistent processing of admissions applications and related materials, application review and admissions decisions; establishes service standards, quality controls, and escalation protocols Oversees effective use and continuous improvement of the admissions CRM and other systems, including workflows, communications, data integrity, reporting, integrations, and user adoption, in collaboration with university admissions and information technology Coordinates campus admissions activities with those of other campus and university departments and the admissions representative network to provide a coordinated student experience from inquiry through enrollment Builds and maintains recruitment pipelines and relationships with high schools, school counselors, employers, alumni, and other university and community partners; represents the university at recruitment and professional events Maintains campus admissions practices, communications, records, and decisions comply with applicable laws, regulations, accreditation standards, and university policies, including requirements related to student records and data privacy Prepares and monitors departmental budget Supervises and develops the department staff, facilitating professional opportunities to improve individual capability and managing performance against job accountabilities, department goals and established university, campus and department policies and procedures Supervises and manages student employees, as necessary, to enhance their academic and professional development Performs other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a bachelor's degree Moderate amount of progressively responsible experience working in college or university admissions, recruitment or enrollment management, including leadership and supervisory responsibilities or other related experience Experience developing and executing recruitment and admissions plans and managing admissions operations Valid U.S. driver's license Proficiency with admissions CRM Preferred Qualifications Master's degree Please Note: Qualified candidates must live or relocate to live within a daily commuting distance of the Charlotte Campus location upon hire. Applications are accepted on an ongoing basis until job posting is closed. Johnson & Wales University is an equal opportunity employer. The university does not illegally discriminate on the basis of any protected class. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnic and national origin, familial status, gender or gender identity, genetic information, military service, national origin, pregnancy and related conditions, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected class. Advertised: 25 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscripti