d sustains relationships with internal and external stakeholders to strengthen available student referral networks for mental health and substance abuse Collaborates with the university clinical team to provide student support through case management, triage and crisis intervention Collaborates with the project director to engage community-based providers and develop formal student referral pathways Serves as the primary program liaison supporting various internal and external meetings, as well as interactions with students, referral organizations and others, as appropriate Collaborates with other university departments to maintain an understanding of internal student referral procedures in an effort to refer students in distress to the appropriate on-campus resources Develops, organizes and implements relevant mental health and substance training and educational programming for the campus community to reduce stigma and increase access to care for university students Organizes and develops social media campaigns surrounding mental health, substance abuse and crisis intervention Supports the program director with long-term program planning Performs other duties as assigned Required Qualifications Minimum of a master's degree Experience working in case management, direct clinical experience, experience working with diverse populations or other related experience Clinical license in Rhode Island Please Note: Qualified candidates must live or relocate to live within a daily commuting distance of the Providence Campus location upon hire. Applications are accepted on an ongoing basis until job posting is closed. Johnson & Wales University is an equal opportunity employer. The university does not illegally discriminate on the basis of any protected class. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnic and national origin, familial status, gender or gender identity, genetic information, military 