    "https://careers.jwu.edu/": {
      "title": "Contact Employer Relations",
      "description": "Home | JWU Careers | Johnson & Wales University skip to main content Apply Now Academics Majors & Programs 3-Year Bachelorâs Degrees Accelerated Masterâs Programs Our Faculty Experiential Education Personalized Learning Admissions Visit Campus Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Transfer Students International Students Online Education Cost & Aid Financial Aid Scholarships & Grants Tuition & Fees Financial Planning Team Net Price Calculator Providence Majors & Programs Life on Campus Visit Providence Colleges Athletics Charlotte Majors & Programs Life on Campus Visit Charlotte Colleges Athletics Info For Future Students Current Students Educators Families Community About JWU Leadership JWU History JWU Magazine Our Alumni Media Center Accreditation Resources News Give Request Info Visit Apply Search Go Search options Search Programs Search Faculty and Staff HIRE JWU Home / JWU Careers Related links Home Post a Job Host an Internship On-Campus Recruitment Sponsorship 100% Grads who participated in experiential education (Charlotte and Providence campuses) 1,134 Students who completed an internship 96.2% Of employers rate JWUâs internship program as good or exceptional At Johnson & Wales University, we believe that learning by doing is one of the most effective and high-impact ways to learn — which is why experiential learning has been woven into all aspects of our education, in and out of the classroom, for more than 100 years. From collecting and analyzing data through research and fieldwork to volunteering with companies and events related to their field of study, JWU’s experiential education program will help students build a strong résumé — and a successful personal life — before they graduate. JWU’s experiential education program puts students on the path to make effective career choices, identify and pursue internships that can help secure employment, and navigate lifelong career direction. Our Students Make Your Search Easy They represent an exceptional pipeline of driven, career-ready professionals who bring valuable industry and transferable skills making an impact at your company— even before they graduate. They know your industry. From their first day at JWU, they’re immersed in your field, working with industry-experienced faculty and a career-focused curriculum targeted to your business. They get advice and an insider's understanding from industry leaders in classroom presentations and workshops, at our career events and through on-campus interviews. They’re professionals, taking advantage of our expertise and career skills training at targeted workshops. They know what to provide during the interview process, including resumes, portfolios and references, and they embody the professionalism you seek in an employee. Most important, they are career ready. Our alumni are making an impact in their field, and leading employers from all industries regularly hire them. How do we know what employers look for? Simple: We ask them. We maintain close relationships with leading companies worldwide. This allows our industry-experienced faculty and team of career experts to stay ahead of what’s happening in your industry, so our students remain among the most outstanding job candidates for your company. We know it’s essential to stay connected to what’s going on in your industry, so we’re involved in national organizations and professional groups to keep our students ahead of the curve as your industry grows and changes. JWU Students Bring You Value We connect you with students for internship, employment, and professional development opportunities to further enhance your recruitment pipeline. Learn more about our academic programs . Contact Employer Relations Give your company the unique advantage of working with a JWU intern or employee. Start working with us as an employer partner by emailing our Experiential Education teams in Providence and Charlotte . When recruiting student interns, there are opportunities to intern in the fall, spring or summer. Internships last for 15 to 16 weeks. We recommend posting your internship six months in advance to recruit the best talent. Academic Semesters are typically Fall (last week of August to mid-December), Spring (January to April) and Summer (May to mid-August). Providence Dianne Compos , 401-598-2144 Charlotte Bryan Mullin , 401-598-1420 Request information Visit Campus Providence Charlotte Start your application Contact us 8 Abbott Park Place, Providence, RI 02903 800-342-5598 A to Z About Academics Academic Calendars Accreditation Admissions Alumni Apply to JWU Athletics Campuses Career Services Catalog Compliance Consumer Information Employment Give to JWU Hire Our Students International Admissions jwuLink Kitchen Academy Media Center POSSIBILITY 2027 Social Directory Terms of Use Tuition & Aid Virtual Tours Wildcat Gear Contact Us Â© Johnson & Wales University Notice of Nondiscrimination Johnson & Wales University (JWU) admits students of or with any age, color, disability, ethnic and national origin, gender, gender identity, genetic information, marital or parental status, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other legally protected category to all the activities, privileges, programs, and rights generally accorded or made available to students at the university. JWU does not discriminate on the basis of age, color, disability, ethnic and national origin, gender, gender identity, genetic information, marital or parental status, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other legally protected status, in administration of its admissions policies, educational policies, loan and scholarship programs, and athletic or any other school-administered programs. Inquiries regarding the university’s nondiscrimination policies may be directed to the university’s Title IX Coordinator. Read the university’s full nondiscrimination notice ."
    }
